.TH mnnn-mcp-add 1  "mnnn-mcp-add 2.25.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-mcp\-add \- Add an external MCP server: `\-\-url URL` (HTTP) or `\-\- COMMAND ARGS…` (stdio)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn mcp add\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-env\fR] [\fB\-\-header\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-token\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add an external MCP server: `\-\-url URL` (HTTP) or `\-\- COMMAND ARGS…` (stdio)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
An HTTP(S) MCP endpoint
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<KEY[=VALUE]>\fR
Environment variables for a stdio server (`KEY=VALUE`, or `KEY` to be asked, hidden)
.TP
\fB\-\-header\fR \fI<NAME[=VALUE]>\fR
HTTP headers (`NAME=VALUE`, or `NAME` to be asked, hidden)
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
A bearer token (`Authorization: Bearer …`); `\-` to be asked, hidden
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write logs to this file instead of stderr (the TUI defaults to <home>/logs/tui.log)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_LOG_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<stream|poll>\fR
How live collaboration reaches peers: `stream` (gRPC streams, the default) or `poll` (requests over the peer connection; for containers). Overrides MUNINN_COLLAB_TRANSPORT and the `net config \-\-collab\-transport` setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
The command (and its arguments) of a stdio server
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.25.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
